术报告现已发布于 arXiv。\n  * `2026/05/18`: 🔥 我们发布了 项目主页，并在 GitHub 和 Hugging Face 上开源了初版推理代码和模型权重。\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nai-that-works/data.json at main · ai-that-works/ai-that-works · GitHub (https://github.com/ai-that-works/ai-that-works/blob/main/data.json)\nciteturn41128search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; When you are deploying heavy LLM workloads or complex pipelines, an unoptimized VM can lead to crippling latency, memory bottlenecks, and ballooning costs that break your application in the real world. ... \"code\": \"https://github.com/hellovai/ai-that-works/tree/main/2026-05-19-feature-flag-everything\"\nWe break down practical techniques to configure your environments, manage resources, and eliminate overhead so your models run flawlessly under pressure.\\n\",\n\n\"event_link\": \"https://luma.com/no-vibes-allowed-performance-eng\",\n\n\"eventDate\": \"2026-05-26T18:00:00Z\",\n\n\"event_type\": \"episode\",\n\n\"media\": {\n\n\"url\": \"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLi60mUelRAbFqfgymVfZttlkIyt0XHZjt\",\n\n\"type\": \"video/youtube\"\n\n},\n\n\"links\": {\n\n\"code\": \"https://github.com/ai-that-works/ai-that-works\"\n\n},\n\n\"season\": 2,\n\n\"episode\": 59,\n\n\"isPast\": true,\n\n\"isWorkshop\": false\n\n},\n\n{\n\n\"folder\": \"2026-05-19-feature-flag-everything\",\n\n\"guid\": \"aitw-058\",\n\n\"title\": \"How AI Agents Can Safely Ship Code to Production\",\n\n\"description\": \"This week, the top headline is vibe coders realizing that they can use feature flags to ship experimental (read: slop) features to production without impacting all customers.\\n\\nShipping code is a lot harder when everything is changing all the time. Feature flags can be a good technique to test various things, but how do you set that up? Do you feature flag new models? New prompts? New harnesses? We'll dive into details here and see where feature flags improve your product delivery vs. just giving you a